{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed for review as Gerrit change 2678, and it is now the PARENT of the three-change stack:\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2678\n\nStack order (parent first): 2678 (this canary fix) -> 2676 (pre-gate guard) -> 2677 (deadline\nrace). Reordered deliberately. 2676 and 2677 had taken `Verified -1` from the canary because\nneither of them fixes it; with 2678 as the parent, every patchset in the stack carries the\ncanary fix and can verify. Verified the reorder is content-preserving: the stack tip's tree hash\nis byte-identical to the tree `make verify` passed on.\n\n`make verify` on the full three-commit stack: 19950 passed, 25 skipped in 31m32s, exit 0, zero\nFAILED lines. The parent commit ALONE (canary fix without the other two) also smoke-tests green\nin a throwaway worktree with the audited binary on PATH: 25 passed, including\ntest_pinned_upstream_canary.\n\nNot submitted — the operator submits.\n\nNote on why the canary job's failure IS patchset-fixable, since this was queried: the workflow\ndefinition comes from trusted main, but its step runs `pip install '.[dev,grounding-terraform]'`\nagainst the CHECKED-OUT PATCHSET, so the patchset's `src/rebar/schemas/` and\n`src/rebar/grounding/` are what the canary exercises. The defect was in those, not in the\nworkflow, so no operator/admin action is needed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788615492809192221,"uuid":"623ff34d-e980-4f41-9308-d8028ee1ad21"}